  },
  "type": "biological",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p>Hibernoids are transgenic-modified humans with heavily altered sleep patterns and metabolic processes. Hibernoids have a decreased need for sleep, requiring only 1-2 hours a day on average. They can also trigger a form of voluntary hibernation, effectively halting their metabolism and need for oxygen. Hibernoids make excellent long-duration space travelers, but these morphs are also favored by personal aides and hypercapitalists with non-stop lifestyles.</p>",
    "reference": "Eclipse Phase Second Edition p. 56",
